{"name":"Beach Umbrella","hex":"#819aaa","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"beach umbrella","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Synonym of parasol (“a small light umbrella used as protection from the sun”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beach_umbrella"}],"entries":[{"title":"Umbrella","blocks":[{"text":"An umbrella is a folding canopy supported by wooden or metal ribs that is mounted on a wooden, metal, or plastic pole. It is usually designed to protect a person against sun or rain. Initially, they were used in warmer countries for shade from the sun, but later evolved to also be used for protection from rain. Etymologically, the term umbrella is to be used when protecting from the sun, but is also commonly used when protecting from rain. Some countries specifically use the words parasol and parapluie to differentiate based on their use. There are also combinations of parasol and parapluie that are called en-tout-cas. A modern hand-held umbrella or parasol may have a black exterior canopy and a silver inner coating, for better protection from both the sun and ultraviolet rays, and may be water-resistant."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/M0354_000727-005_1.jpg/330px-M0354_000727-005_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Umbrella"},{"title":"Beach","blocks":[{"text":"A beach is a landform alongside a body of water which consists of loose particles. The particles composing a beach are typically made from rock, such as sand, gravel, shingle, pebbles, etc., or biological sources, such as mollusc shells or coralline algae. Sediments settle in different densities and structures, depending on the local wave action and weather, creating different textures, colors and gradients or layers of material."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Beach_at_Fort_Lauderdale.jpg/330px-Beach_at_Fort_Lauderdale.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beach"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Zenkoji-Nagano.JPG/500px-Zenkoji-Nagano.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Zenkoji-Nagano.JPG/1280px-Zenkoji-Nagano.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Zenkoji-Nagano.JPG/500px-Zenkoji-Nagano.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Woman holding a parapluie at Zenkō-ji, Nagano, Japan","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AZenkoji-Nagano.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Hatshepsut_temple4_b.jpg/500px-Hatshepsut_temple4_b.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Hatshepsut_temple4_b.jpg/1280px-Hatshepsut_temple4_b.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Hatshepsut_temple4_b.jpg/500px-Hatshepsut_temple4_b.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Relief of an Egyptian umbrella. These were used as sunshade and fan alike (flabellum).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHatshepsut_temple4_b.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Relief_of_Xerxes_at_Doorway_of_his_Palace%2C_Persepolis%2C_Iran.jpg/500px-Relief_of_Xerxes_at_Doorway_of_his_Palace%2C_Persepolis%2C_Iran.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Relief_of_Xerxes_at_Doorway_of_his_Palace%2C_Persepolis%2C_Iran.jpg/500px-Relief_of_Xerxes_at_Doorwa